<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">24 April in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 24 April, from 1184 BCE to 1990.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/troy" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/troy.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1184 BCE <span class="tih-ago">842 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Troy falls, according to ancient Greek reckoning</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Greek chronographers, notably <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eratosthenes">Eratosthenes</a>, dated the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/troy">Troy</a> to 1184 BCE, and later writers placed it in late April. The legend, told in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/homer">Homer</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virgil">Virgil</a>, shaped European literature for millennia.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1800 CE <span class="tih-ago">226 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Congress establishes the Library of Congress</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">President John Adams signed the act moving the government to Washington and setting aside $5,000 for books for Congress. The collection became one of the largest libraries in the world.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1877 CE <span class="tih-ago">149 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Russia declares war on the Ottoman Empire</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> went to war in support of the Balkan Christians. The peace that followed made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> and Montenegro fully independent and created an autonomous <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1915 CE <span class="tih-ago">111 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ottoman authorities arrest Armenian leaders in Constantinople</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Hundreds of Armenian intellectuals and community leaders were rounded up and deported, most later killed. The date marks the start of the Armenian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genocide">genocide</a>, in which around a million people died.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1916 CE <span class="tih-ago">110 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Irish rebels launch the Easter Rising in Dublin</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Irish Volunteers and the Citizen Army seized the General Post Office and proclaimed an Irish Republic. The Rising was crushed within a week, but the executions that followed turned opinion towards independence.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1990 CE <span class="tih-ago">36 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Space shuttle Discovery launches the Hubble Space Telescope</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Hubble was carried into orbit by Discovery and deployed the next day. A flaw in its mirror was corrected in 1993, after which it transformed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylonian-astronomy">astronomy</a>.</p></div></li></ol>
